# Signal Field UI (this project)

Before UI/visual work, read [`docs/design.md`](docs/design.md) (§1 Philosophy + checklist §10).

## Must
- Clarity · deference · depth (P1–P10)
- One accent family (`signal` / `--primary`) — never a second brand purple
- Cards only for interaction; no hero overlays; subtract until meaning breaks
- Focus-visible, AA contrast, hit targets ≥44px where practical; honor `prefers-reduced-motion`
- For service briefs: follow §1.5 + [`docs/recommend-map.md`](docs/recommend-map.md) → 1 primary + 2 alts

## Never
- Purple→indigo on white; cream + terracotta + display serif; broadsheet pastiche
- Glow / neon / glassmorphism card farms; emoji chrome
- Inter / Roboto / Arial / system-ui as the *expressive* face when a kit pairing is chosen
- Silently renaming token roles or forking accent meaning per page

## SurviveEnglish default lean
Primary mix ≈ `precise-quiet` (signal-teal · plex · default). Soft-product and day-editorial are alts. See recommend-map.
